Manufacture of Organic Fine Chemicals, BREF OFC (@ic-fine-organics: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_0DH473049K4WX7HAAY1P7SDS3K
European Commission, Joint Research Centre. Manufacture of Organic Fine Chemicals, BREF OFC. adopted August 2006. [Official reference and full-text access](https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/reference/manufacture-organic-fine-chemicals).

A full technical treatment of multipurpose/batch organic production, including pharmaceutical and other specialty products, intermediates, solvents, isolation, site operations and emissions.

Read the complete book for the advanced batch/fine-chemical study. Follow chemistry, development methods, thermal behavior, solvent/separation work, cleaning/changeover, quality, waste and the transfer from a reaction experiment to a repeatable process. Case families include more than pharmaceuticals; exact plant-specific know-how can remain absent.

Identity, stated scope, date and official access were checked on 29 October 2026. This is a dated technical reference, not a claim that every described plant, technology or legal reference is current everywhere. Preserve its attribution, actual reuse notice and third-party exceptions; public access is not described as a blanket CC licence. Full-text or automated inspection limits are distinguished where relevant. No book, figure, industrial data or associated media is bundled. The official full PDF has 456 file pages. It is a technical process source, not a claim of current clinical or medicinal-product regulatory guidance.

